{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779395914,"nonce":"VA+4rZa/mKd/7N2XxwJuHwe0sX8=","title":"Studio dimension propagation engine and parameter sync","message":"Parent: 0258fac\nDepends on: 974b9ba\n\n## Summary\nImplement the authoring-side dimension propagation engine that derives component parameter updates from graph wires and Task Data bindings, applies unambiguous updates by default, and reports conflicts without hiding runtime mutation.\n\n## UX decision\nDimension sync is on by default for Studio-authored scenarios. When a user wires or binds values whose schemas imply a component dimension, Studio updates the affected editable parameter immediately if the constraint is unambiguous. The update is visible as an authoring change, undoable, and traceable to its source. The worker/runtime still validates the final saved spec and never silently fixes dimensions during execution.\n\n## Interaction pattern\n- On connect or Task Data binding change, run a pure `deriveDimensionConstraints` pass before saving the graph update.\n- If exactly one value is implied for an auto-managed param, update the graph spec and show the param as synced rather than merely edited.\n- If a user manually edits a synced dimension, record it as a manual override and stop auto-updating that param until the user resumes sync.\n- If constraints conflict, do not overwrite the user's value. Keep or reject the attempted connection based on existing connection policy, but always surface one clear conflict issue naming the param, current value, inferred values, and source edges/bindings.\n- Unknown dimensions never auto-propagate. They should create warnings/explanations, not guessed sizes.\n\n## Covered propagation rules\n- Task Data direct binding to `Network.input` updates `Network.input_size` from the Task Data sample-view last axis when known.\n- Delayed reach Task Data bound through `task_mux` updates `Network.input_size` from the mux output sum: target position `2` + hold/go cue `1` + target shown `1` = `4` for the default DelayedReaches slice.\n- `Network.output -\u003e PointMass.force` and `Network.output -\u003e TwoLinkArm.force` update `Network.out_size` to `2`.\n- `Network.output -\u003e Arm6MuscleRigidTendon.excitation` updates `Network.out_size` to `6`.\n- `Network.output -\u003e PointMass8MuscleRelu.excitation` updates `Network.out_size` to `2 * n_pairs` when `n_pairs` is known.\n- Outer `Network.input_size`/`out_size` changes propagate into the generated Network subgraph cell/readout params.\n\n## Data model\nStore sync state in Studio-authored metadata rather than runtime-only local state. The minimum useful shape is:\n- scenario/workspace setting: auto dimension sync enabled/disabled;\n- managed param records keyed by graph path and param path;\n- provenance: source schema ids, source labels, inferred value, updated_at, and whether the value is automatic or manual override.\n\n## Out of scope\n- General symbolic algebra beyond integer last-axis sizes and simple sums/products listed above.\n- Auto-adapter insertion, reshape/cast nodes, or hidden compatibility shims.\n- Provider/live execution behavior beyond preserving final-spec validation.\n\n## Done criteria\n- A pure constraint derivation function is unit-tested independently of React state.\n- Store mutations apply derived updates on connect, task-binding changes, graph normalization, and relevant param edits.\n- Updates are undoable via existing graph history.\n- Existing graphs with invalid or conflicting dimensions remain inspectable and produce conflicts rather than destructive rewrites.\n- Worker tests continue to verify final spec mismatches fail clearly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}